#uuid "e73acfeb-8e27-55c3-ab0b-f7bd350b0723" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049309 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049309 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049309 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050002 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049309 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049309 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049309 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049309 #edb/ref 1031 "Absolute Value Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049309 #edb/ref 1033 451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049309 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "eb56b359-bf3c-5bc4-a26b-629e05c1d464" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050448 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050448 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050448 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049005 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050448 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050448 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050448 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186192634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050448 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186192635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050448 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186192636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050448 #edb/ref 1031 "Further Absolute Value Equations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050448 #edb/ref 1033 4029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050448 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "49d2d213-870d-5feb-be49-bffbb6cbe24a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186191269 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186191269 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186191269 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ee0c8bd5-1086-5d70-85b2-9d89fb5fe3c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192592 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14220" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192592 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the absolute value equation\n$-3 \\mid 1-x \\mid -2 = -8$.\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$\\mid 1-x|=k$\n\nWhat is the value of $k$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192592 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b3b99d07-5914-578b-9aaf-f028ada5bee0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192592 #edb/ref 1074 "We can rearrange the equation to isolate the absolute value on the left-hand side:\n\nFirst, we add $2$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 - x & -2 &= -8 \\\\ -3 & 1 - x & -2 + 2|=-8 + 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 - x & |=-6\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-3{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3 \\mid 1 - x \\mid &= -6 \\\\\n\\frac{-3 \\mid 1 - x\\begin{vmatrix}}{-3} &= \\frac{-6}{-3} \\\\ \\frac{-3 \\mid 1 - x\\end{vmatrix}}{-3}|= 2 \\\\\n\\mid 1 - x \\mid &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=2$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192593 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14223" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192593 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following equations has *no* solution?\n\n1. $\\mid 1-x \\mid = -5$\n2. $\\mid 1-x \\mid + 5 = 2$\n3. $\\mid 1-x \\mid = 3$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192593 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "89382e45-4e78-554f-88e1-2bbf281617e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192593 #edb/ref 1074 "An absolute value equation has no solution if, when the absolute value is isolated on the left-hand side, the right-hand side is negative.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each equation in turn:\n\n- Equation I *has no solution*. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is *negative*.\n- Equation II *has no solution*. To see this, we first isolate the absolute value on the left-hand side as follows:\n$\\mid 1 - x \\mid + 5|= 2; \\mid 1 - x \\mid |=-3$\nSince the right-hand side is *negative*, this equation has *no* solution.\n- Equation III has a solution. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is non-negative.\n\nTherefore, the answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192594 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14228" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192594 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $2 \\mid 2a - 4 \\mid - 7 = 13$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192594 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "de2efe4f-e236-5fb2-bc46-eb037ecf26b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192594 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\begin{vmatrix}2a - 4 & -7 &= 13 \\\\ 2 & 2a - 4\\end{vmatrix}|= 20 \\\\\n\\mid 2a - 4 \\mid &= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $\\mid 2a-4 \\mid = 2a-4$, we obtain:\n$\\mid 2a - 4 \\mid |= 10; 2a - 4|= 10; 2a|= 14; a|= 7$\n- If $\\mid 2a-4 \\mid = -(2a-4)$, we obtain:\n$\\mid 2a - 4 \\mid |= 10; - (2a - 4)|= 10; - 2a + 4|= 10; - 2a|= 6; a|=-3$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $a=-3$ and $a=7$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1039 "Isolating an Absolute Value Expression" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192634 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5bc2c576-4f7c-5b4a-8c78-8a41420fdcce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192635 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192635 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192635 #edb/ref 1039 "Absolute Value Equations With No Solution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192635 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192635 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "94d6a2aa-4288-51dc-8944-cf9490812ad2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192636 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192636 #edb/ref 1039 "Rearranging and Solving an Absolute Value Equation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192636 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192636 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "15f03573-42ee-50d4-acdf-e2ee05d3e7e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192907 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186193425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192907 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186193426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192907 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186193427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192907 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186193428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192907 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186193429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192907 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186193430 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192907 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192907 #edb/ref 1045 "Further Absolute Value Equations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192907 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186193425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192907 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192907 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "157f57f7-71ad-5178-b6a1-cb1065e17520" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193245 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186191269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193245 #edb/ref 1069 "q-212480" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193245 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the absolute value equation\n$2 - \\mid x + 2|= 7$.\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$\\mid x + 2|=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193245 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e5a53e17-d1d0-5fa9-8d04-0b459a7ec9bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193425 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193425 #edb/ref 1061 144049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193425 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b4b80cf6-ac66-5b80-8e9a-84e34ac2fd5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193425 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186193943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193426 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193426 #edb/ref 1061 144050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193426 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6e54dac3-7257-553a-9281-d652e78869f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193426 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193427 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193427 #edb/ref 1061 144054 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193427 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1f7f7690-789e-59b6-a31a-f699646aed1e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193427 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186193944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193428 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193428 #edb/ref 1061 144055 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193428 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dd2c5b77-7fcb-5443-969e-13f565428281" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193428 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186193945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193429 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193430 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193429 #edb/ref 1061 144056 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193429 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cc568d38-8ed7-5e05-b47d-35fcd03f33e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193429 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193430 #edb/ref 1061 144059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193430 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9aebc5c1-cf53-5a78-8700-b622cd65203b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193430 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193943 #edb/ref 1064 "A valuable skill to master when dealing with absolute value equations is to isolate the absolute value expression first.\n\nTo isolate an absolute value expression, we treat it like a variable in a linear equation.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's consider the following absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n2 \\mid x-1 \\mid + 4 = 8\n$$\n\nWe aim to isolate the $\\mid x-1 \\mid$ term on the left-hand side.\n\nWe start by subtracting $4$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & x - 1 & + 4 &= 8 \\\\ 2 & x - 1 & + 4 - 4|= 8 - 4 \\\\ 2 & x - 1 & |= 4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2 \\mid x - 1 \\mid &= 4 \\\\\n\\frac{2 \\mid x - 1\\begin{vmatrix}}{2} &= \\frac{4}{2} \\\\ \\frac{2 \\mid x - 1\\end{vmatrix}}{2}|= 2 \\\\\n\\mid x - 1 \\mid &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd that's it! We've successfully isolated the absolute value expression in our equation.\n\nLet's consider another example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193943 #edb/ref 1065 8824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193943 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "640fe647-93cb-5b1a-8707-6c53032d81ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193943 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193944 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's consider the following absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\vert x \\vert = -4\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The absolute value of any number is *always* positive or zero.\n- So, there is no number whose absolute value is negative.\n- Therefore, this equation $\\mid x \\mid = -4$ has **no solution.**\n\nAnother way of understanding this is to recall that the absolute value of a number represents the number's distance from the origin, and distances cannot be negative." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193944 #edb/ref 1065 8826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193944 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b272858e-f85c-5daa-ad70-c87f7a3b792f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193944 #edb/ref 1067 "Recognizing Equations With No Solution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193945 #edb/ref 1064 "So, we know that the following equation has no solution:\n\n$$\n\\vert x \\vert = -4\n$$\n\nLet's see what happens when we blindly apply the usual process of solving our equation:\n\n- if $\\mid x \\mid = x$, we get\n$\\mid x \\mid |=-4; x|=-4$.\n- if $\\mid x \\mid = -x$, we get\n$\\mid x \\mid |=-4; - x|=-4; x|= 4$.\n\nSo, the usual process has given us the \"solutions\"\n\n$$\nx= {\\color{red}{-4}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nx= {\\color{blue}{4}}\n$$\n\nHowever, neither of these values satisfies the original equation!\n\nFor example, by substituting\n\n$$\nx = {\\color{blue}{4}}\n$$\n\ninto the original equation, we get a *false statement!*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid x \\mid &= -4 \\\\\n\\mid 4 \\mid &= -4 \\\\\n4 &= -4\\cdot\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe key takeaway is that it's essential to check that the right-hand side is positive (or zero) *before* applying the usual solution process." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193945 #edb/ref 1065 8827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193945 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ea3bc553-4605-5ceb-8f0b-e788bb67414a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193945 #edb/ref 1067 "Attempting to Solve an Equation With No Solution" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
